<!-- Block renderer for blocks_catalog_page.

     Despite the .json name (kept so the existing instance view is reused) this
     emits the block's RAW HTML, not JSON. Deliberate: a block view contains
     quotes, newlines and <script> bodies, and wrapping that in a JSON string
     needs an escaper Parsley does not offer. HTML round-trips losslessly and
     fetch().text() ignores the content type.

     ?block=<view name>   required — resolves /-/block/<block>.html
     ?variant=<7-zuid>    optional — omitted falls through to the default

     The caller must revive the <script type="text/babel"> tags in the response;
     innerHTML does not execute scripts. blocks_catalog_page does this the same
     way the loader's CurrentView does.

     NB: this is an HTML comment. Parsley parses comments too, so a Parsley
     tag must never appear inside one — writing one here would error the whole
     response. (A Parsley-style comment would not help: the bang-prefixed form
     is this codebase's output modifier, so it would be read as a variable.) -->
{{if {get_var.block} }}{{if {get_var.variant} }}{{ block('/-/block/{get_var.block}.html?variant={get_var.variant}') }}{{else}}{{ block('/-/block/{get_var.block}.html') }}{{end-if}}{{end-if}}
